# Dear Wallet rules

You are building Dear Wallet, a soft Y2K iPhone-first money diary. Source of truth: docs/BUILD_SPEC.md, docs/SCREENS.md, docs/COPY.md, src/theme/tokens.json, and the pixel specs in design-source/canvas/*.dc.html.

## Stack
- React Native + Expo (development build, expo-router, TypeScript strict). Install packages with `npx expo install`.
- Styling with NativeWind classes. Colours only from the token classes: bg-bg1 bg-bg2 bg-c1..bg-c5 bg-surface border-outline text-ink bg-btn text-btn-text, plus /opacity variants. For react-native-svg and Reanimated use tokens(palette) from src/theme/theme.ts.
- Never hard-code a hex colour in a component. Exceptions: sticker art and the HOLO constant, which are fixed by design.
- Data: expo-sqlite + drizzle locally, Supabase as the sync target. Money is integer cents. IDs are client-generated uuids.
- Animations: Reanimated on the UI thread, transforms and opacity only. Gestures: react-native-gesture-handler.

## Design rules
- Fonts: Pacifico for titles 20 pt+, Nunito 600-900 for text, Pixelify Sans 500/600 for amounts, window titles and UPPERCASE tags (tracking 0.06em). Never put amounts in script.
- Borders 2 pt in outline colour, hard offset shadows (no blur), radii from tokens.json.
- Every interactive element is a Pressable with accessibilityRole and accessibilityLabel, and at least 44 × 44 pt including hitSlop.
- Selected states use a border or the btn colour, never a pale card tint alone.
- Must work from 375 × 667. Below 740 pt window height use the compact values from the matching .dc.html file.
- Respect reduced motion (single 200 ms fade), haptics and sound settings everywhere.

## Product rules
- Logging needs only amount + name and must work offline with no spinner.
- Every completed action triggers the reward within 300 ms.
- No shame: never write "failed", "broke", "overspent", "streak", "missed", or guilt notifications. Copy is short, warm, lightly lowercase (see COPY.md).
- Bought it after all removes an item from totals and is undoable; earned milestones are never revoked.
- Diary is private. No analytics SDKs.

## Working style
- Build one screen or component per change, matching the named canvas state.
- Prefer small, typed, testable functions in src/features/*; keep UI components presentational.
- If the spec is silent, ask or leave a TODO with a clear question rather than inventing behaviour.
